      "rationale": "The statements carry the exact premise. Compactness is equivalent to BPI over ZF (SUP 29-35; B1 181-189). Completeness holds over ZF+BPI for every set P, and the scheme is equivalent to BPI over ZF (FB 248-264). The justifications are written in full: the compactness bridge in both directions (A1 291-350); finite support and closed schemata, Boolean-valued soundness, the quotient, the free property and the premise filter (FBA 2-362); and the avoidance filter, the single BPI ultrafilter extension, the truth lemma, completeness, compactness and the converse from the scheme to BPI (FBA 364-477)."
