      "rationale": "W17 109-149 (proof W17A 87-143) restricts the decision procedures to finite encoded inputs over coded atoms and shows the answers do not depend on the coding. W17 151-159 (proof W17A 145-176) shows that uncountable or non-well-orderable atom sets have no coding. W17 202-234 (proof W17A 321-391) shows that finite checks give only the compactness hypothesis, that the coded case is choice-free through thm:prop-compactness, and that the arbitrary scheme is BPI-equivalent. SUP 213-233 limits thm:p02-decidability to finite inputs. FB 19-23, 262-263 and 277-291 separate the countable choice-free theorem (R2665 45-66) and the decision procedures from the arbitrary-language scope. The core distinction does not depend on the computability theorems at W17 171-188, whose sketched dependencies are disclosed at W17 342-352."
